        "rawClasses": [
          "iron-man-1"
        ],
        "rawHtml": "<h1>Iron Man <em>(2008)</em></h1>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        <strong class=\"iron-man\">Tony Stark</strong>, who has inherited the defense contractor <em>Stark\r\n                            Industries</em> from his father Howard Stark, is in war-torn Afghanistan with his friend and\r\n                        military liaison, Lieutenant Colonel <strong class=\"war-machine\">James Rhodes</strong>, to\r\n                        demonstrate the new \"Jericho\" missile. After the demonstration, the convoy is ambushed and Stark\r\n                        is\r\n                        critically wounded by a missile used by the attackers: one of his company's own. He is captured\r\n                        by a\r\n                        terrorist group called the <em>Ten Rings</em>. <strong class=\"secundary\">Yinsen</strong>, a\r\n                        fellow\r\n                        captive doctor, implants an <strong>electromagnet</strong> into Stark's chest to keep the\r\n                        shrapnel\r\n                        shards that wounded him from reaching his heart and killing him. Stark and Yinsen secretly build\r\n                        a\r\n                        small, powerful electric generator called an <strong>arc reactor</strong> to power Stark's\r\n                        electromagnet and a <strong>prototype suit of powered armor</strong> to aid in their escape.\r\n                        <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Yinsen</strong> sacrifices himself to divert them while the suit\r\n                        powers\r\n                        up. The armored Stark battles his way out.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        After being rescued by Rhodes, Stark returns\r\n                        home (<strong class=\"jarvis\">Jarvis</strong> is his robotic assitant) and announces that his\r\n                        company\r\n                        will <strong>cease manufacturing weapons</strong>. <strong class=\"enemy\">Obadiah Stane</strong>,\r\n                        his\r\n                        father's old partner and the company's manager, advises Stark that this may ruin Stark\r\n                        Industries\r\n                        and his father's legacy. In his home workshop, Stark builds in secret a <strong>sleeker, more\r\n                            powerful version of his improvised armor suit</strong> as well as a <strong>more powerful\r\n                            arc\r\n                            reactor</strong>. Personal assistant <strong class=\"pepper\">Pepper Potts</strong> places the\r\n                        original reactor inside a small glass showcase. <strong class=\"secundary\">Happy</strong> is his\r\n                        \"bodyguard\". At a charity event held by Stark Industries, reporter <strong\r\n                            class=\"secundary\">Christine Everhart</strong> informs Stark that his company's weapons were\r\n                        <strong>double-selling</strong> to the Ten Rings. Potts meets with Agent <strong\r\n                            class=\"coulson\">Phil Coulson</strong> of <em>S.H.I.E.L.D.</em>, to inform him of Stane's\r\n                        activities.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Stane ambushes Stark at his home and steals the arc reactor from his chest and also\r\n                        exterminates the <em class=\"presumably dead\">Ten Rings</em>. The last fight carries Stark\r\n                        and Stane to the top of the Stark Industries building, and Stark instructs Potts to overload the\r\n                        <strong>large\r\n                            arc reactor</strong> powering the building killing him. The next day, at a press conference,\r\n                        Stark defies suggestions from S.H.I.E.L.D. and publicly admits to being <strong\r\n                            class=\"iron-man\">\"Iron Man\"</strong>.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        <strong class=\"fury\">Nick Fury</strong> visits Stark at\r\n                        home and explains that he wants to discuss the <em>\"Avenger Initiative\".</em>\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "<strong class=\"iron-man\">Tony Stark</strong>, who has inherited the defense contractor <em>Stark Industries</em> from his father Howard Stark, is in war-torn Afghanistan with his friend and military liaison, Lieutenant Colonel <strong class=\"war-machine\">James Rhodes</strong>, to demonstrate the new \"Jericho\" missile. After the demonstration, the convoy is ambushed and Stark is critically wounded by a missile used by the attackers: one of his company's own. He is captured by a terrorist group called the <em>Ten Rings</em>. <strong class=\"secundary\">Yinsen</strong>, a fellow captive doctor, implants an <strong>electromagnet</strong> into Stark's chest to keep the shrapnel shards that wounded him from reaching his heart and killing him. Stark and Yinsen secretly build a small, powerful electric generator called an <strong>arc reactor</strong> to power Stark's electromagnet and a <strong>prototype suit of powered armor</strong> to aid in their escape. <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Yinsen</strong> sacrifices himself to divert them while the suit powers up. The armored Stark battles his way out.",
          "After being rescued by Rhodes, Stark returns home (<strong class=\"jarvis\">Jarvis</strong> is his robotic assitant) and announces that his company will <strong>cease manufacturing weapons</strong>. <strong class=\"enemy\">Obadiah Stane</strong>, his father's old partner and the company's manager, advises Stark that this may ruin Stark Industries and his father's legacy. In his home workshop, Stark builds in secret a <strong>sleeker, more powerful version of his improvised armor suit</strong> as well as a <strong>more powerful arc reactor</strong>. Personal assistant <strong class=\"pepper\">Pepper Potts</strong> places the original reactor inside a small glass showcase. <strong class=\"secundary\">Happy</strong> is his \"bodyguard\". At a charity event held by Stark Industries, reporter <strong class=\"secundary\">Christine Everhart</strong> informs Stark that his company's weapons were <strong>double-selling</strong> to the Ten Rings. Potts meets with Agent <strong class=\"coulson\">Phil Coulson</strong> of <em>S.H.I.E.L.D.</em>, to inform him of Stane's activities.",
          "Stane ambushes Stark at his home and steals the arc reactor from his chest and also exterminates the <em class=\"presumably dead\">Ten Rings</em>. The last fight carries Stark and Stane to the top of the Stark Industries building, and Stark instructs Potts to overload the <strong>large arc reactor</strong> powering the building killing him. The next day, at a press conference, Stark defies suggestions from S.H.I.E.L.D. and publicly admits to being <strong class=\"iron-man\">\"Iron Man\"</strong>.",
          "<strong class=\"fury\">Nick Fury</strong> visits Stark at home and explains that he wants to discuss the <em>\"Avenger Initiative\".</em>"
        ],
