        "rawHtml": "<h1>Iron Man 2 <em>(2010)</em></h1>\r\n                    <h5>Stark Expo 2010</h5>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        In Russia <strong class=\"enemy\">Ivan Vanko</strong>, whose father, <strong\r\n                            class=\"enemy dead\">Anton\r\n                            Vanko</strong>, a former <em>Stark Industries</em> employee, has just died, begins building\r\n                        a\r\n                        <strong>miniature arc reactor</strong> similar to Stark's. Six months later, <strong\r\n                            class=\"iron-man\">Stark</strong> uses his Iron Man suit for peaceful means, resisting\r\n                        government\r\n                        pressure to <strong>sell his designs</strong>. Later, Stark learns that the <strong>palladium\r\n                            core</strong> is slowly poisoning him, and he cannot find a substitute. Stark appoints his\r\n                        personal assistant <strong class=\"pepper\">Pepper Potts</strong> as <strong>CEO</strong> of Stark\r\n                        Industries and hires Stark employee <strong class=\"black-widow\">Natalie Rushman</strong> to\r\n                        replace\r\n                        her as his personal assistant. Stark competes in the Monaco Historic Grand Prix, where he\r\n                        is attacked in the middle of the race by Vanko. Stark dons his armor and defeats Vanko.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Stark's rival, <strong class=\"enemy\">Justin Hammer</strong>, fakes Vanko's death and asks him to\r\n                        build a\r\n                        line of <strong>armored suits</strong>. Stark's best friend, <strong class=\"war-machine\">James\r\n                            Rhodes</strong> confiscates <strong>one of the armors for the U.S. Air Force.</strong>\r\n                        <strong class=\"fury\">Nick Fury</strong>, director of <em>S.H.I.E.L.D.</em>, approaches Stark,\r\n                        revealing\r\n                        that \"Rushman\" is Agent <strong class=\"black-widow\">Natasha Romanoff</strong> and that Howard\r\n                        Stark\r\n                        was a S.H.I.E.L.D. founder. Fury gives Stark some of his <strong>father's old material</strong>.\r\n                        Tony discovers a hidden message, with the aid of his A.I., <strong\r\n                            class=\"jarvis\">J.A.R.V.I.S.</strong>, he <strong>synthesizes a new element, ending his\r\n                            palladium\r\n                            dependency</strong> (with the help of <strong>Captain America's shield prototype</strong> ).\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        At the Expo, Hammer unveils Vanko's armored drones, led by Rhodes in a <strong>heavily\r\n                            weaponized\r\n                            version of the prototype armor</strong>. Stark arrives to warn Rhodes, but Vanko takes\r\n                        remote\r\n                        control of all the drones and Rhodes' armor and attacks Stark. Hammer soon gets arrested for\r\n                        breaking Vanko out of prison while Romanoff and Stark's bodyguard Happy Hogan go after Vanko at\r\n                        Hammer's factory. <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Vanko</strong> commits suicide by blowing up his\r\n                        suit,\r\n                        along with the defeated drones.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        At a debriefing, Fury informs Stark that because of his\r\n                        difficult personality, S.H.I.E.L.D. intends to use him only as a <strong>consultant</strong>.\r\n\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "In Russia <strong class=\"enemy\">Ivan Vanko</strong>, whose father, <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Anton Vanko</strong>, a former <em>Stark Industries</em> employee, has just died, begins building a <strong>miniature arc reactor</strong> similar to Stark's. Six months later, <strong class=\"iron-man\">Stark</strong> uses his Iron Man suit for peaceful means, resisting government pressure to <strong>sell his designs</strong>. Later, Stark learns that the <strong>palladium core</strong> is slowly poisoning him, and he cannot find a substitute. Stark appoints his personal assistant <strong class=\"pepper\">Pepper Potts</strong> as <strong>CEO</strong> of Stark Industries and hires Stark employee <strong class=\"black-widow\">Natalie Rushman</strong> to replace her as his personal assistant. Stark competes in the Monaco Historic Grand Prix, where he is attacked in the middle of the race by Vanko. Stark dons his armor and defeats Vanko.",
          "Stark's rival, <strong class=\"enemy\">Justin Hammer</strong>, fakes Vanko's death and asks him to build a line of <strong>armored suits</strong>. Stark's best friend, <strong class=\"war-machine\">James Rhodes</strong> confiscates <strong>one of the armors for the U.S. Air Force.</strong> <strong class=\"fury\">Nick Fury</strong>, director of <em>S.H.I.E.L.D.</em>, approaches Stark, revealing that \"Rushman\" is Agent <strong class=\"black-widow\">Natasha Romanoff</strong> and that Howard Stark was a S.H.I.E.L.D. founder. Fury gives Stark some of his <strong>father's old material</strong>. Tony discovers a hidden message, with the aid of his A.I., <strong class=\"jarvis\">J.A.R.V.I.S.</strong>, he <strong>synthesizes a new element, ending his palladium dependency</strong> (with the help of <strong>Captain America's shield prototype</strong> ).",
          "At the Expo, Hammer unveils Vanko's armored drones, led by Rhodes in a <strong>heavily weaponized version of the prototype armor</strong>. Stark arrives to warn Rhodes, but Vanko takes remote control of all the drones and Rhodes' armor and attacks Stark. Hammer soon gets arrested for breaking Vanko out of prison while Romanoff and Stark's bodyguard Happy Hogan go after Vanko at Hammer's factory. <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Vanko</strong> commits suicide by blowing up his suit, along with the defeated drones.",
          "At a debriefing, Fury informs Stark that because of his difficult personality, S.H.I.E.L.D. intends to use him only as a <strong>consultant</strong>."
        ],
