        "rawHtml": "<h1>MARVEL'S Daredevil <em>(Season 1 / 2015)</em> </h1>\r\n                    <p><strong class=\"daredevil\">Matt Murdock</strong> at the age of nine was hit with a truck filled\r\n                        with\r\n                        hazardous waste <strong>blinding him while simultaneously enhancing his remaining senses to\r\n                            superhuman levels</strong>. After his father died, a man named <strong\r\n                            class=\"secundary\">Stick</strong> taught him how to manipulate his powers and training him in\r\n                        Martial Arts. He went to college and befriended <strong class=\"secundary\">Foggy Nelson</strong>.\r\n                        The\r\n                        two of them found <em>the Nelson and Murdock law firm</em>. <strong class=\"enemy\">Wilson\r\n                            Fisk</strong> had a traumatic, unstable childhood. Wilson kills his father with a hammer to\r\n                        death. Even well into his adult years, his father’s dark lessons in cruelty, power, respect, and\r\n                        control helped mold him into the man he is today, <strong class=\"enemy\">the Kingpin</strong>.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        <strong class=\"mcu\">After the Battle of New York, Hell's Kitchen is struggling to\r\n                            recover.</strong>\r\n                        Crime is in an all-time high due to the rise of a crime syndicate: utilizing drugs, weapons, and\r\n                        gangs to de-value the local property; to remake them into new crime-controlled buildings.\r\n                        Their very first client, <strong class=\"secundary\">Karen Page</strong>, grateful for the duo’s\r\n                        save,\r\n                        decides to work with them. Murdock continued his vigilantism and Wilson Fisk, falls in love to\r\n                        art\r\n                        curator, <strong class=\"enemy\">Vanessa Marianna</strong>. Meanwhile, Nelson and Page had been\r\n                        secretly working\r\n                        with <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Ben Urich</strong> to build a credible case against Fisk.\r\n                        <strong class=\"claire\">Claire</strong> is a nurse who's been helping Matt, knowing his\r\n                        indentity,\r\n                        Foggy then too.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        After gathering enough credible evidence against Fisk and the death of the Yakuza mafia's leader\r\n                        <strong class=\"enemy presumably-dead enemy\">Nobu</strong>, Murdock and the police was able to\r\n                        charge\r\n                        Fisk for criminal activity and was arrested. Finally donning the Daredevil costume, Murdock\r\n                        personally takes on Fisk as Daredevil, and wins after a fairly difficult fight. <strong>\r\n                            Fisk</strong> is now arrested\r\n                        and in jail; Marianna escaped and left the city. Murdock continued on his guardianship and\r\n                        vigilantism over the city as the <strong class=\"daredevil\">Daredevil</strong>.\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "<strong class=\"daredevil\">Matt Murdock</strong> at the age of nine was hit with a truck filled with hazardous waste <strong>blinding him while simultaneously enhancing his remaining senses to superhuman levels</strong>. After his father died, a man named <strong class=\"secundary\">Stick</strong> taught him how to manipulate his powers and training him in Martial Arts. He went to college and befriended <strong class=\"secundary\">Foggy Nelson</strong>. The two of them found <em>the Nelson and Murdock law firm</em>. <strong class=\"enemy\">Wilson Fisk</strong> had a traumatic, unstable childhood. Wilson kills his father with a hammer to death. Even well into his adult years, his father’s dark lessons in cruelty, power, respect, and control helped mold him into the man he is today, <strong class=\"enemy\">the Kingpin</strong>.",
          "<strong class=\"mcu\">After the Battle of New York, Hell's Kitchen is struggling to recover.</strong> Crime is in an all-time high due to the rise of a crime syndicate: utilizing drugs, weapons, and gangs to de-value the local property; to remake them into new crime-controlled buildings. Their very first client, <strong class=\"secundary\">Karen Page</strong>, grateful for the duo’s save, decides to work with them. Murdock continued his vigilantism and Wilson Fisk, falls in love to art curator, <strong class=\"enemy\">Vanessa Marianna</strong>. Meanwhile, Nelson and Page had been secretly working with <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Ben Urich</strong> to build a credible case against Fisk. <strong class=\"claire\">Claire</strong> is a nurse who's been helping Matt, knowing his indentity, Foggy then too.",
          "After gathering enough credible evidence against Fisk and the death of the Yakuza mafia's leader <strong class=\"enemy presumably-dead enemy\">Nobu</strong>, Murdock and the police was able to charge Fisk for criminal activity and was arrested. Finally donning the Daredevil costume, Murdock personally takes on Fisk as Daredevil, and wins after a fairly difficult fight. <strong> Fisk</strong> is now arrested and in jail; Marianna escaped and left the city. Murdock continued on his guardianship and vigilantism over the city as the <strong class=\"daredevil\">Daredevil</strong>."
        ],
