        "rawHtml": "<h1>MARVEL'S Luke Cage <em>(Season 1 / 2016)</em> </h1>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        <strong class=\"luke-cage\">Luke Cage</strong> keeps a low profile as a sweeper at ex-gangster\r\n                        <strong class=\"secundary\">Henry \"Pop\" Hunter</strong>'s barbershop, and as a dishwasher at crime\r\n                        boss\r\n                        <strong class=\"enemy\">Cornell \"Cottonmouth\" Stokes</strong>' nightclub, Harlem's Paradise. NYPD\r\n                        detectives <strong class=\"secundary\">Misty Knight</strong> and <strong class=\"enemy\">Rafael\r\n                            Scarfe</strong> investigate a crime and impound the <em>Hammer Industries</em> weapons that\r\n                        Stokes was selling. With help from <strong class=\"enemy\">\"Shades\" Alvarez</strong>, who works\r\n                        for\r\n                        Stokes' supplier <strong class=\"enemy\">Diamondback</strong> and also the suppor oft his cousin\r\n                        <strong class=\"enemy\">Mariah Dillard</strong>, a councilwoman. They want to own Harlem. Stokes\r\n                        men\r\n                        kill <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Pop</strong> accidentally. Stokes goes to the restaurant\r\n                        where\r\n                        Cage is living and fires a missile at the building. Cage pulls himself and his landlady out of\r\n                        the\r\n                        rubble, and <strong>reveals his abilities and name to the media.</strong>\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        <strong class=\"claire\">Claire Temple</strong> arrives in Harlem to visit her mother. Shades\r\n                        reveals\r\n                        to Stokes a new type of weapon, <strong class=\"mcu\">the Judas bullet, built from alien metal and\r\n                            based on a prototype stolen from Hammer Industries</strong>, that could kill Cage. Dillard\r\n                        kills\r\n                        <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Stokes</strong>, and Shades helps her frame Cage for the murder. With\r\n                        Stokes unable to afford it, Diamondback use a Judas bullet to kill Cage himself in exchange for\r\n                        control of Harlem. Claire meets up with Cage. <strong class=\"enemy\">Stryker</strong> is\r\n                        Diamondback,\r\n                        Luke's half-brother. Seeking revenge confronts Cage on a sidestreet.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Claire convinces Cage to get <strong class=\"enemy\">Burstein's</strong> help, and they find the\r\n                        doctor living in hiding. He places Cage in <strong>acid that should soften his skin</strong> and\r\n                        allow them to remove the shrapnel. He and Claire look through the files on him and learn that\r\n                        <strong class=\"secundary\">Reva</strong> had known about Seagates's fights, and was assessing\r\n                        Cage\r\n                        with the intention of putting him through Burstein's procedure as a test subject. Stryker\r\n                        appears\r\n                        wearing a <strong>Hammer's powered suit</strong> which allows him to match Cage's strength and\r\n                        invulnerability. Cage tasks Knight to go after Dillard and Alvarez while he engages Stryker.\r\n                        Federal\r\n                        marshals arrest Cage for his escape from Seagate. Claire kisses him before he leaves, and\r\n                        <strong>promises to call a <strong class=\"daredevil\">good lawyer</strong> that she\r\n                            knows</strong>. A\r\n                        friend finds the <strong>files to clear Cage's name</strong> in the barbershop. Dillard re-opens\r\n                        Harlem's Paradise with Alvarez by her side, and Knight watching them. Claire considers taking up\r\n                        self-defense lessons. A hospitalized Stryker is visited by Burstein.\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "<strong class=\"luke-cage\">Luke Cage</strong> keeps a low profile as a sweeper at ex-gangster <strong class=\"secundary\">Henry \"Pop\" Hunter</strong>'s barbershop, and as a dishwasher at crime boss <strong class=\"enemy\">Cornell \"Cottonmouth\" Stokes</strong>' nightclub, Harlem's Paradise. NYPD detectives <strong class=\"secundary\">Misty Knight</strong> and <strong class=\"enemy\">Rafael Scarfe</strong> investigate a crime and impound the <em>Hammer Industries</em> weapons that Stokes was selling. With help from <strong class=\"enemy\">\"Shades\" Alvarez</strong>, who works for Stokes' supplier <strong class=\"enemy\">Diamondback</strong> and also the suppor oft his cousin <strong class=\"enemy\">Mariah Dillard</strong>, a councilwoman. They want to own Harlem. Stokes men kill <strong class=\"secundary dead\">Pop</strong> accidentally. Stokes goes to the restaurant where Cage is living and fires a missile at the building. Cage pulls himself and his landlady out of the rubble, and <strong>reveals his abilities and name to the media.</strong>",
          "<strong class=\"claire\">Claire Temple</strong> arrives in Harlem to visit her mother. Shades reveals to Stokes a new type of weapon, <strong class=\"mcu\">the Judas bullet, built from alien metal and based on a prototype stolen from Hammer Industries</strong>, that could kill Cage. Dillard kills <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Stokes</strong>, and Shades helps her frame Cage for the murder. With Stokes unable to afford it, Diamondback use a Judas bullet to kill Cage himself in exchange for control of Harlem. Claire meets up with Cage. <strong class=\"enemy\">Stryker</strong> is Diamondback, Luke's half-brother. Seeking revenge confronts Cage on a sidestreet.",
          "Claire convinces Cage to get <strong class=\"enemy\">Burstein's</strong> help, and they find the doctor living in hiding. He places Cage in <strong>acid that should soften his skin</strong> and allow them to remove the shrapnel. He and Claire look through the files on him and learn that <strong class=\"secundary\">Reva</strong> had known about Seagates's fights, and was assessing Cage with the intention of putting him through Burstein's procedure as a test subject. Stryker appears wearing a <strong>Hammer's powered suit</strong> which allows him to match Cage's strength and invulnerability. Cage tasks Knight to go after Dillard and Alvarez while he engages Stryker. Federal marshals arrest Cage for his escape from Seagate. Claire kisses him before he leaves, and <strong>promises to call a <strong class=\"daredevil\">good lawyer</strong> that she knows</strong>. A friend finds the <strong>files to clear Cage's name</strong> in the barbershop. Dillard re-opens Harlem's Paradise with Alvarez by her side, and Knight watching them. Claire considers taking up self-defense lessons. A hospitalized Stryker is visited by Burstein."
        ],
