        "rawHtml": "<h1>Inhumans <em>(Season 1 / 2017)</em></h1>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Attilan is ruled by <em>the Inhuman Royal Family</em>, at the top of which are King <strong\r\n                            class=\"secundary\">Black Bolt</strong> and Queen <strong class=\"secundary\">Medusa</strong>.\r\n                        Other\r\n                        members of the Royal Family include Black Bolt's brother <strong class=\"enemy\">Maximus</strong>,\r\n                        who\r\n                        actually lost all opportunity of displaying superpowers after his Terrigenesis, Medusa's sister\r\n                        <strong class=\"secundary\">Crystal</strong>, and Black Bolt's cousins <strong\r\n                            class=\"secundary\">Karnak, Triton and Gorgon.</strong>\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Maximus intends to overthrow his brother and tries to rally the population of Attilan by\r\n                        promising\r\n                        that he will lead them to Earth. The members of the Royal Family attempt to reunite, but face\r\n                        challenges of their own in the island of Hawaii. When Maximus forces is being defeated, the\r\n                        Inhuman\r\n                        Royal Family declare themselves ready to return to Attilan and confront him. However, Maximus\r\n                        reveals that he has enacted a failsafe which could lead to Attilan's destruction. Fearing such a\r\n                        fate, Black Bolt instructs Medusa and Crystal to arrange for the evacuation of the city to\r\n                        Earth.\r\n                    </p>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        Black Bolt confronts his brother one last time, and is shocked when Maximus reveals that he has\r\n                        a\r\n                        share of responsibility in their parents' death. Black Bolt abandons <strong\r\n                            class=\"presumably-dead enemy\">Maximus</strong> on the Moon. The Royal Family then prepare to\r\n                        lead the population of Attilan on a new settlement on Earth, where the Inhumans originated.\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Attilan is ruled by <em>the Inhuman Royal Family</em>, at the top of which are King <strong class=\"secundary\">Black Bolt</strong> and Queen <strong class=\"secundary\">Medusa</strong>. Other members of the Royal Family include Black Bolt's brother <strong class=\"enemy\">Maximus</strong>, who actually lost all opportunity of displaying superpowers after his Terrigenesis, Medusa's sister <strong class=\"secundary\">Crystal</strong>, and Black Bolt's cousins <strong class=\"secundary\">Karnak, Triton and Gorgon.</strong>",
          "Maximus intends to overthrow his brother and tries to rally the population of Attilan by promising that he will lead them to Earth. The members of the Royal Family attempt to reunite, but face challenges of their own in the island of Hawaii. When Maximus forces is being defeated, the Inhuman Royal Family declare themselves ready to return to Attilan and confront him. However, Maximus reveals that he has enacted a failsafe which could lead to Attilan's destruction. Fearing such a fate, Black Bolt instructs Medusa and Crystal to arrange for the evacuation of the city to Earth.",
          "Black Bolt confronts his brother one last time, and is shocked when Maximus reveals that he has a share of responsibility in their parents' death. Black Bolt abandons <strong class=\"presumably-dead enemy\">Maximus</strong> on the Moon. The Royal Family then prepare to lead the population of Attilan on a new settlement on Earth, where the Inhumans originated."
        ],
