        "rawHtml": "<h1>MARVEL'S Luke Cage <em>(Season 2 / 2018)</em> </h1>\r\n                    <p>\r\n                        After clearing his name, <strong class=\"luke-cage\">Luke Cage</strong> has become a celebrity on\r\n                        the\r\n                        streets of Harlem with a reputation as bulletproof as his skin. But being so visible has only\r\n                        increased his need to protect the community and find the limits of who he can and can’t save.\r\n                        With\r\n                        the rise of a formidable new foe and <strong class=\"enemy\">Shades</strong>, <strong\r\n                            class=\"enemy dead\">Mariah Dillard</strong> is killed by her daughter in prison. Luke is forced\r\n                        to\r\n                        confront the fine line that separates a hero from a villain with the help on the way from\r\n                        <strong class=\"claire\">Claire Temple</strong> (they finally broken up due to differences),\r\n                        <strong class=\"secundary\">Misty Knight</strong> with a robotic arm created by RAND <strong\r\n                            class=\"iron-fist\">Danny Rand</strong> and <strong class=\"colleen-wing\">Colleen</strong>. Luke\r\n                        struggles with the best way to attack the problems facing his community, and in the end he\r\n                        resolves\r\n                        that the best path forward is to deputize himself as the veritable sheriff of Harlem, operating\r\n                        out\r\n                        of the same place both Mariah and the late Cottonmouth once called their home.\r\n                    </p>",
        "paragraphs": [
          "After clearing his name, <strong class=\"luke-cage\">Luke Cage</strong> has become a celebrity on the streets of Harlem with a reputation as bulletproof as his skin. But being so visible has only increased his need to protect the community and find the limits of who he can and can’t save. With the rise of a formidable new foe and <strong class=\"enemy\">Shades</strong>, <strong class=\"enemy dead\">Mariah Dillard</strong> is killed by her daughter in prison. Luke is forced to confront the fine line that separates a hero from a villain with the help on the way from <strong class=\"claire\">Claire Temple</strong> (they finally broken up due to differences), <strong class=\"secundary\">Misty Knight</strong> with a robotic arm created by RAND <strong class=\"iron-fist\">Danny Rand</strong> and <strong class=\"colleen-wing\">Colleen</strong>. Luke struggles with the best way to attack the problems facing his community, and in the end he resolves that the best path forward is to deputize himself as the veritable sheriff of Harlem, operating out of the same place both Mariah and the late Cottonmouth once called their home."
        ],
